    {
      "id": "find_67bfd43a9081400e",
      "workspace_id": "ws_03abec922ce74395",
      "summary": "Most likely cause: r184 checkout 503s come from application connection-pool exhaustion (DB_POOL_MAX=4), not from the database.",
      "detail": "Inference tying the observations together: r184 error rate ~40% (find_bdd8be12049749aa) matches r184's reduced pool of 4 per pod (find_122fad635ca64392); r184 pods are pool-saturated with pool_wait_p95_ms=3000, equal to CHECKOUT_TIMEOUT_MS=3000, producing ~300 pool-wait timeouts/min (find_f9bfdcfb99e04917); the database stayed healthy with 181+ free connections (find_0bea8b50bf5f4db5), so the constraint is the per-pod client pool, not DB capacity. Confirm: after removing r184 traffic or restoring DB_POOL_MAX=24, r184 pool_wait_timeouts and 503s should fall. Refute: 503s persist with an unconstrained pool, or another r184 behavior (e.g. a slow query path) shows up in logs. Not independently confirmed by an error-log artifact; confidence is from correlational evidence.",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "source_artifact_id": "art_21329a1f063e4eed",
      "created_by_actor_id": "agt_4c8b57d1b1a04528",
      "created_by_actor_type": "agent",
