  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "dec_948d10692b3f4595",
      "workspace_id": "ws_03abec922ce74395",
      "summary": "Immediately shift all order-api traffic in us-east-1 off order-api-r184 back to r183 (abort the partial rollout) and keep the rollout paused until r184 is fixed.",
      "rationale": "r184 carries ~40% 503s while r183 stays near baseline, and the 503s began when r184 took traffic; pausing the rollout at 09:22Z left r184 still serving 25% and did not remove the failing revision. Restoring all traffic to the known-good r183 is the least-risk way to stop customer impact now. The underlying r184 defect (DB_POOL_MAX=4 causing pool-wait timeouts at the 3000ms checkout timeout) should be corrected before any resume. This is a proposal only; it is not approved and no production change has been authorized in this exercise. Do not execute a rollback or config change without explicit approval.",
